Intermediate Fluid Mechanics — James Liburdy (@fd-liburdy: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_45KKWKB7DTN9MMQ951P62JHH5N
James Liburdy. Intermediate Fluid Mechanics, Oregon State University, 16 September 2021. [Complete book](https://open.oregonstate.education/intermediate-fluid-mechanics/).

Read all eleven chapters with independent derivations and exercises. They develop mathematical tools, Bernoulli reasoning, potential flow and panel methods, viscous and boundary-layer models, integral methods, turbulence and CFD basics. The book provides the engineering continuation after an introductory fluid course; it does not replace compressible or multiphase study.

The publisher states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 except where otherwise noted. It now marks the book archived and no longer updated. Use the actual contents list, which includes chapter XI on CFD, rather than treating an earlier ten-chapter description as the current inventory. Online text and PDF remain external references.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
